{"course":"engineering-mathematics-i","departments":["*"],"faculty":"engineering","format":1,"key":"engineering/engineering-mathematics-i","questions":[{"cognitive_patterns":["Pure Mathematical"],"correct_option_id":"b","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Using the power rule, d/dx(x^n) = n*x^(n-1), so d/dx(x²) = 2x.","id":"q001","information_types":["Computation (skill)"],"options":[{"id":"a","text":"x"},{"id":"b","text":"2x"},{"id":"c","text":"x²"},{"id":"d","text":"2"}],"prompt":"What is the derivative of x² with respect to x?"},{"cognitive_patterns":["Pure Mathematical"],"correct_option_id":"c","difficulty":1,"explanation":"sin(90°) = 1, the maximum value of the sine function.","id":"q002","information_types":["Computation (skill)"],"options":[{"id":"a","text":"0"},{"id":"b","text":"0.5"},{"id":"c","text":"1"},{"id":"d","text":"undefined"}],"prompt":"What is the value of sin(90°)?"},{"cognitive_patterns":["Pure Mathematical"],"correct_option_id":"b","difficulty":1,"explanation":"2x + 4 = 10 -> 2x = 6 -> x = 3.","id":"q003","information_types":["Computation (skill)"],"options":[{"id":"a","text":"x = 2"},{"id":"b","text":"x = 3"},{"id":"c","text":"x = 4"},{"id":"d","text":"x = 7"}],"prompt":"Solve for x: 2x + 4 = 10"},{"cognitive_patterns":["Pure Mathematical"],"correct_option_id":"b","difficulty":2,"explanation":"For a 2x2 matrix, the determinant is calculated as (a*d) - (b*c).","id":"q004","information_types":["Computation (skill)"],"options":[{"id":"a","text":"a+d - b+c"},{"id":"b","text":"ad - bc"},{"id":"c","text":"ab - cd"},{"id":"d","text":"ac - bd"}],"prompt":"The determinant of the 2x2 matrix [[a,b],[c,d]] is:"},{"cognitive_patterns":["Pure Mathematical"],"correct_option_id":"c","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The integral of 2x with respect to x is x² + C, reversing the power rule of differentiation.","id":"q005","information_types":["Computation (skill)"],"options":[{"id":"a","text":"x + C"},{"id":"b","text":"2x² + C"},{"id":"c","text":"x² + C"},{"id":"d","text":"x²/2 + C"}],"prompt":"Evaluate the integral of 2x dx."},{"cognitive_patterns":["Pure Mathematical"],"correct_option_id":"b","difficulty":1,"explanation":"log10(100) = 2, since 10^2 = 100.","id":"q006","information_types":["Computation (skill)"],"options":[{"id":"a","text":"1"},{"id":"b","text":"2"},{"id":"c","text":"10"},{"id":"d","text":"100"}],"prompt":"What is the value of log10(100)?"},{"cognitive_patterns":["Pure Mathematical"],"correct_option_id":"b","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The interior angles of any triangle always sum to 180°.","id":"q007","information_types":["Computation (skill)"],"options":[{"id":"a","text":"90°"},{"id":"b","text":"180°"},{"id":"c","text":"270°"},{"id":"d","text":"360°"}],"prompt":"The sum of the interior angles of a triangle is:"},{"cognitive_patterns":["Pure Mathematical"],"correct_option_id":"b","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The quadratic formula x = (-b ± sqrt(b²-4ac)) / 2a solves any equation of the form ax² + bx + c = 0.","id":"q008","information_types":["Computation (skill)"],"options":[{"id":"a","text":"ax + b = 0"},{"id":"b","text":"ax² + bx + c = 0"},{"id":"c","text":"ax³ + b = 0"},{"id":"d","text":"a/x + b = 0"}],"prompt":"The quadratic formula is used to solve equations of the general form:"}]}